   use.

3. Mods, fan works and derived works. You may make and share mods
   (changed or new data files, such as scenarios, ship classes, themes
   and tuning), community mods, fan works (stories, art, videos, guides),
   and works derived from the Software, including changed builds, as long
   as you:
   a. credit the Author, for example "Based on Ghost Boat by Anthony
      Giacalone", where people will see it;
   b. say that your work is not official; and
   c. do not charge for it.

4. Hosting. You may host the Software for a small group, such as a
   community server or your friends, so they can play it over the
   network, as long as:
   a. no more than 20 people are connected to it at once;
   b. you do not charge for access, which includes requiring a
      donation, subscription or other payment to play; and
   c. you keep this licence available to the people who play.

5. What needs permission. You may not sell the Software, a mod, a fan
   work or a derived work, host it for more than 20 people at once or
   for a fee, or use any of it in a commercial product, without the
   Author's written permission.

6. Succession. When the Author dies, or becomes unable to manage his
   affairs as certified by a physician or a court, the Software is
   licensed to everyone under the GNU General Public License, version 3
   or (at your option) any later version. From that day, the terms of
   that licence replace sections 2 to 5.

7. No warranty. The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of
   any kind. The Author is not liable for any claim or damage arising
